        The high-speed rotary atomizer wheel operates with an expansive peripheral velocity of 169.6 m/s, delivering high centrifugal shear that atomizes feed droplets down to Dv50 = 52 μm. Radial flight trajectory calculations confirm that droplet surfaces desaturate and solidify in 0.48 seconds, well before reaching the chamber cylinder wall (0.82 seconds flight time). Deposit accumulation remains below self-heating thresholds with active pneumatic knockers.
