      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-surface-soft border border-hairline">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-ink mb-1.5 flex items-center gap-1.5">
          <span class="text-primary font-mono">03.</span>
          Frank-Kamenetskii Self-Heating
        </h4>
        <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed">
          Thick wall deposits (&gt; 10 mm) act as thermal insulation. Inside the cake, exothermic Maillard browning and carbohydrate caramelization generate heat faster than it can conduct away into the metal wall or cooling air. When the Frank-Kamenetskii parameter &delta; exceeds the critical threshold (&delta;_cr &approx; 0.88), spontaneous thermal runaway occurs, forming pyrophoric embers.
        </p>
